{
  "info": {
    "name": "AI Tour Guide Backend (Dev 2 scope)",
    "_postman_id": "b7e1a1a0-0a1a-4a2a-9a1a-a1a1a1a1a1a1",
    "description": "Visitor-facing API: content retrieval (§9), chat grounding (§10), and narration/audio (§11).\n\nSetup before using this collection:\n1. `npm run seed` then `npm run dev` from the `backend/` folder.\n2. Fill in the collection variables `roomId`, `itemId`, and `museumSlug` with real values from your seeded DB, e.g.:\n   `SELECT id FROM \"Room\" WHERE \"legacyId\"='room_1';`\n   `SELECT id FROM \"Item\" WHERE \"legacyId\"='room_1_treaty';`\n3. Run \"POST /chat\" once first to populate `answerId` automatically (its response is captured into the collection variable by a test script on that request), then the two `/narrate/answer/:answerId` requests will work.\n\nAll error responses share one envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"message\": string, \"code\": string, \"requestId\": string } }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000" },
    { "key": "museumSlug", "value": "adwa-museum" },
    { "key": "roomId", "value": "REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ROOM_UUID" },
    { "key": "itemId", "value": "REPLACE_WITH_REAL_ITEM_UUID" },
    { "key": "answerId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["health"] },
            "description": "Liveness + DB connectivity check. Returns 200 with { status, dbLatencyMs, version }."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Visitor Content (§9)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /waypoint/:id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/waypoint/{{roomId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["waypoint", "{{roomId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Returns a room with its items. 404 if the room doesn't exist or belongs to a suspended museum (indistinguishable from nonexistent, by design)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /waypoint/:id (404 - unknown room)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/waypoint/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["waypoint", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]
            },
            "description": "Expect 404 NOT_FOUND."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /museums/:slug",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/museums/{{museumSlug}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["museums", "{{museumSlug}}"]
            },
            "description": "Returns { id, name, slug, ticketRequired }."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /museums/:slug (404 - unknown slug)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/museums/does-not-exist",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["museums", "does-not-exist"]
            },
            "description": "Expect 404 NOT_FOUND."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Chat (§10)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "POST /chat - Case 2 (free-form, no itemId)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  const answerId = body.audioUrl.replace('/narrate/answer/', '');",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('answerId', answerId);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"waypointId\": \"{{roomId}}\",\n  \"question\": \"What happened in this room?\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/chat", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["chat"] },
            "description": "The model classifies which item (if any) the question is about and grounds the answer against room + item context. Saves the returned answerId into the `answerId` collection variable for the narrate requests below."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /chat - Case 1 (item-specific, with itemId)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"waypointId\": \"{{roomId}}\",\n  \"itemId\": \"{{itemId}}\",\n  \"question\": \"Tell me more about this.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/chat", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["chat"] },
            "description": "Grounds strictly on the tapped item's detailText. Response echoes matchedItemId + imageUrl for that exact item."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /chat - repeat question (cached:true expected)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"waypointId\": \"{{roomId}}\",\n  \"question\": \"What happened in this room?\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/chat", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["chat"] },
            "description": "Send the exact same waypointId+question as the first Case 2 request. Response should have \"cached\": true and the same answer/audioUrl, with no LLM call made."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /chat - 400 (blank question)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"waypointId\": \"{{roomId}}\",\n  \"question\": \"   \"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/chat", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["chat"] },
            "description": "Expect 400 VALIDATION_ERROR."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /chat - 404 (unknown waypointId)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"waypointId\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"question\": \"Hello?\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/chat", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["chat"] },
            "description": "Expect 404 NOT_FOUND."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Narration / Audio (§11)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /narrate/room/:roomId",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/narrate/room/{{roomId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["narrate", "room", "{{roomId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Cold path: synthesizes the room's narrationScript, streams audio/mpeg back, and persists roomAudioUrl for next time (redirects on subsequent calls once a real object-storage URL exists)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /narrate/answer/:answerId",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/narrate/answer/{{answerId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["narrate", "answer", "{{answerId}}"]
            },
            "description": "Run a POST /chat request first so `answerId` is populated automatically. Streams (or redirects to) the audio for that specific cached chat answer."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /narrate/answer/:answerId (404 - unknown id)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/narrate/answer/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["narrate", "answer", "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]
            },
            "description": "Expect 404 NOT_FOUND."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
